.Dd $Mdocdate: September 7 2026 $
.Dt OPENBARRC 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openbarrc
.Nd openbar status bar configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This manual page describes the
.Xr openbar 1
configuration file.
.Pp
The configuration syntax follows the keyword style of
.Xr cwm 1 ,
with directives separated by whitespace from their arguments.
Comment lines start with a hash mark
.Pq Sq # .
Arguments containing whitespace should be surrounded by double
.Pq \&"
or single
.Pq '
quotes; a quoted argument must not be followed by other characters.
.Pp
The following options are accepted:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic barheight Ar pixels
Set the height of the status bar in pixels, between 12 and 60.
The default is 24.
.It Ic color barbg Ar color
Set the background colour of the bar.
The default is
.Dq #CCCCCC
.Pq the cwm active border colour .
.It Ic color barfg Ar color
Set the foreground
.Pq text
colour of the bar.
The default is
.Dq #000000 .
.It Ic color urgent Ar color
Set the colour used for urgent elements (currently the battery
segment at or below 15% charge).
The default is
.Dq #FC8814
.Pq the cwm urgency border colour .
.It Ic fontname Ar font
Set the font used for bar text.
The
.Ar font
argument is an
.Xr Xft 3
font pattern.
The default is
.Dq sans-serif:pixelsize=14:bold
.Pq the same default font as cwm .
.It Ic gap Ar top bottom left right
Define a gap in pixels at each edge of the screen.
Exactly four non-negative values are required.
The bar window is placed within this gap so that it does not overlap
other screen-edge elements.
The default is
.Dq 0 0 0 0 .
.It Ic interface Ar name
Set the network interface name used to read the private IPv4
address.
The name must be at most 15 characters and may contain letters,
digits, underscore, dash and dot.
.It Ic logo Ar text
Set the text displayed as the bar logo, at most 127 characters.
This field is required.
.It Ic show Ar widget
Enable the given status widget.
.It Ic hide Ar widget
Disable the given status widget.
.El
.Pp
Available widget names for
.Ic show
and
.Ic hide :
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It hostname
System hostname.
.It date
Current date and time.
.It cpu
CPU clock speed and temperature.
.It mem
Free physical memory in MB.
.It load
1-minute load average.
.It bat
Battery charge percentage.
.It net
Public IPv4, IPv6 and private IPv4 addresses.
.It vpn
WireGuard VPN status.
.El
.Pp
All widgets are disabled by default.
When a directive occurs several times, the last occurrence wins.
Unknown keywords are reported and ignored; malformed values, unknown
widget names and unknown colour slots are fatal errors.
Diagnostics include the file name and line number.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.openbarrc" -compact
.It Pa ~/.openbarrc
Default per-user configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/openbarrc
System-wide configuration file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
# Minimal openbar configuration
fontname "sans-serif:pixelsize=14:bold"
color barbg "#CCCCCC"
color barfg "#000000"
color urgent "#FC8814"
barheight 24
gap 0 0 0 0
logo OpenBar
interface iwm0
show hostname
show date
show cpu
show mem
show load
show net
show vpn
hide bat
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cwm 1 ,
.Xr openbar 1 ,
.Xr Xft 3 ,
.Xr cwmrc 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file format first appeared in
.Ox .
